WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.002
[music playing]

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.638
NARRATOR: Dr. Colleen
Darnell hunts for clues

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.074
to solve the mystery of
why dozens of pharaohs

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:11.010
were removed from
their original tombs,

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:14.247
and reburied in
an unmarked grave.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.215
[music playing]

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.952
Could this ancient
papyrus hold the answer?

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.353
COLLEEN DARNELL: One of the
more remarkable documents

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.992
to survive from ancient Egypt is
a transcript of the confessions

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.328
of a tomb robber.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:32.031
NARRATOR: The papyrus was
long ago torn down the middle.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:36.870
The two halves now live
in different museums.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:39.739
But by bringing the
pieces together,

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:43.109
Colleen can decode the ancient
confessions of a New Kingdom

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.512
tomb robber named
Amenpanufer, who

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:50.984
broke into the tomb of a pharaoh
named Sobekemsaf the second.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.954
COLLEEN DARNELL: We
took our copper tools

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:59.192
and we broke into its
very inner chamber,

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.995
and we know that they're going
through the mummies themselves

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:06.599
because they talk about
a piece of gold jewelry

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.234
at the neck of the king.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.642
NARRATOR: Amenpanufer
admits to digging a tunnel

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:19.512
into the tomb of the pharaoh.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:24.984
Once inside, he took as
much gold as he could carry,

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.719
but he was caught.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.489
For his crimes, a
brutal punishment.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:33.259
Sentenced to death by impaling.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:36.062
This tomb robbery,
and others like it,

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:39.299
alarms New Kingdom authorities.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.267
Their pharaoh's
mummies, so sacred

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.771
to the ancient
Egyptians, aren't safe.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.173
The authorities take action.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.477
COLLEEN DARNELL: In order to
safeguard the royal mummies,

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.146
they were moved,
rewrapped, and buried

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.948
together in an unmarked tomb.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.652
We know that the plan worked.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.187
By moving them from
the Valley of the Kings

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:04.324
to an unmarked
tomb, they survived

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.759
for thousands of years.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:10.530
[music playing]

